{"id": "DfHzMKtIMRO", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "How many times should you walk around HANUMAN? 🙏 And Krishna, Murugan, the Navagraha? Part 3, the gods you asked for.\n\nIn Part 2 we gave the rounds from one verse of the Narasimha Purana (Devi 1, Ganesha 3, Vishnu 4, Surya 7, Shiva half). You asked for more gods, so here they are:\n\n🔹 Krishna: 4, the same as Vishnu. The same verse says “four for Keshava”. This is the ONLY one of the four with a Purana verse behind it.\n🔹 Murugan: 6, from a count verse many South Indian families recite (Ganesha 1, Surya 2, Shiva 3, Vishnu 4, Devi 5, Skanda 6). Nobody we found can say which text it comes from. Some temples do 7.\n🔹 Navagraha: 9, the common custom (some do 7 or 11).\n🔹 Hanuman: 3 in the popular lists, and 11 at many Hanuman temples, often as a vow for a wish.\n\nCustoms differ from temple to temple, so when in doubt, follow your temple’s priest. 🛕\n\nWant your kids to know our gods? Our picture books, Books 1–3, are a set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n📌 Save this for your next temple visit and send it to someone who always asks “how many rounds?”\n💬 Hanuman: 3 or 11? Tell us what YOUR temple does!\nPart 4: Shani, Lakshmi, Ayyappa. Follow so you don’t miss it.\n\n#Hanuman #Pradakshina #Parikrama #Krishna #Murugan Navagraha HinduTemple TempleRules SanatanaDharma Hinduism Bajrangbali Kartikeya HinduRituals RishiKatha IndianCulture", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793370672, "like_count": 2407, "comment_count": 19, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2205008323747762a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.552, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMCRlBE9YTXca508CdhpCBhzzmQZ1oGw4d8OLelzMExjhOKYOZqvJNRiw92Acac9kN6PXINWUpG6OPJgl4zJsRGqTCe